# lint-staged formats what is staged - TypeScript, JSON, CSS and YAML, never Markdown. docs/*.md and
# docs/*.mdx mirror the product repo's docs/ byte for byte, so .lintstagedrc.json names no Markdown pattern
# and .prettierignore excludes *.md and *.mdx as the second line of defence.
# --no-stash: lint-staged's default backup goes through git stash create/store, and the house rule bans any
# git stash, for any reason - the stack is shared by every checkout and session. Without it lint-staged
# still hides a partially staged file's unstaged changes, through a patch file of its own (17.5.1
# gitWorkflow.js, prepare); what goes is only the backup, and with it the undo when a task fails.
# --relative --max-arg-length 8000: Windows caps a command line at 8,191 characters, and lint-staged
# splits a long file list only when --max-arg-length is set (17.5.1 getSpawnedTasks.js; unset, it never
# chunks). Relative paths keep each chunk short. A 91-file commit failed without them on 2026-09-25.
yarn lint-staged --no-stash --relative --max-arg-length 8000
